# Fork sync exclusion manifest — consumed by script/fork-sync.sh.
#
# Three directive kinds, one glob per line, `#` starts a comment:
#
#   keep-deleted: <glob>   Paths the fork permanently deletes. On every sync,
#                          upstream modifications to these are resolved as
#                          deletion, and ANY file matching the glob that the
#                          merge introduces (including brand-new upstream
#                          files) is removed from the merge result.
#
#   take-theirs: <glob>    Regenerable artifacts the fork does not maintain.
#                          A both-modified conflict on these is resolved to
#                          upstream's version.
#
#   regenerate: <glob>     Regenerable files requiring post-checkout rebuild.
#                          Checkout upstream's version, run the rebuild command
#                          for that file's ecosystem to reconcile it with the
#                          fork's manifest deltas, then stage the result INTO the
#                          merge commit (never as a follow-up commit).
#                          Dispatch is keyed on the matched file's basename, not
#                          the glob: bun.lock -> `bun install`, Cargo.lock ->
#                          `cargo metadata`. This repo is Bun-only; the basename
#                          rule keeps the manifest spec shared with polyglot forks.
#
# Keep this list explicit and reviewed. Do not widen a glob to cover a
# path the fork actually keeps.

# --- Upstream ops/workflow machinery: never restored (commit e11e21e69c).
# --- The fork runs no GitHub-hosted jobs; CI belongs to cloudhome.
keep-deleted: .github/CODEOWNERS
